[38;2;124;124;124mcharacteristic?"[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a knowledge question about mathematics. Let me think about this [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcarefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe Birch and Swinnerton-Dyer (BSD) conjecture is about elliptic curves over [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnumber fields (characteristic 0). The question asks whether it's known in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpositive characteristic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about what "BSD conjecture in positive characteristic" means. In [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpositive characteristic, we have elliptic curves over global fields of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcharacteristic p, i.e., function fields of curves over finite fields.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor elliptic curves over function fields of curves over finite fields (global [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfunction fields), there is an analog of the BSD conjecture. This is actually a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtheorem! The BSD conjecture for elliptic curves over function fields was proved [0m[38;2;124;124;124mby Artin (for genus 0, i.e., rational function fields in some cases), and more [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgenerally by Tate, and the full result is due to work of several people.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me recall the precise history:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m1. For elliptic curves over function fields of curves over finite fields, the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mBSD conjecture is known. This was proved essentially by:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - Artin (1920s) for some cases over F_q(t)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - Tate (work in the 1960s, published later) - proved the rank part[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - The full BSD conjecture (including the leading coefficient formula) for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124melliptic curves over function fields was proved by combining work of Tate (rank [0m[38;2;124;124;124mequality), and Milne/Gapushkin for the leading coefficient.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me be more precise. The BSD conjecture for abelian varieties over [0m[38;2;124;124;124mfunction fields of curves over finite fields:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- The "rank part" (algebraic rank = analytic rank) was proved by Tate.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- The full conjecture (including the leading coefficient) was proved by Milne [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(for the case where the base field is finite, i.e., the function field case) in [0m[38;2;124;124;124mhis 1972 paper, building on work of Tate.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, I need to be more careful. Let me recall:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe BSD conjecture analog for function fields:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- For elliptic curves over global function fields, the BSD conjecture is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtheorem.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Tate proved the rank equality (the order of vanishing of L(E,s) at s=1 equals [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe Mordell-Weil rank) in his 1960s work.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- The full BSD formula (leading coefficient) was proved by Milne in "On the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124marithmetic of abelian varieties" (1972) or similar, using the Tate-Shafarevich [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgroup finiteness results.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, more precisely:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Artin proved BSD for some elliptic curves over F_q(t) in his thesis (1924).[0m
